    "heading": "Name the decision and the queue owner",
    "body": "In the client co-branded campaign approval workflow, a co-branded campaign proposed for a client arrives before anyone confirms the client, the period, or the responsible queue. A client co-branded campaign approval request can be complete and still not be approved, so the note separates the request from the decision. If two client co-branded campaign approval sources disagree, the note says which system of record will govern the answer. Review pass 1.1: the account team files the client co-branded campaign approval evidence.\n\nThe client co-branded campaign approval working file joins the creative draft, the client approval, the brand review, and the publication record on one case reference so the decision can be rebuilt. A client co-branded campaign approval case without a named owner is treated as unassigned, even when a document is already attached. The client co-branded campaign approval queue shows the promised response time, the current owner, and the next action. Review pass 1.2: the account team files the client co-branded campaign approval evidence."
